    "end": "Nor is she.",
    "caption": "Look who's still dancing at breakfast.\n\nGrace is 1.3 million people in soft, low hills, with gravity light enough that nobody's feet ever get tired. The rule is older than anyone can remember: the band plays until the last dancer sits down. Musicians retire young. Wedding invitations give a start time and a polite estimate.\n\nOn my first night I was the last one on the floor, looking for my shoe. The band played until I found it.\n\n(On Earth, the story goes, the first dance at a wedding comes from the old formal balls, where the guests of honour opened the floor. On Grace, it's the last dance everyone remembers.)\n\nWhich song would keep you on your feet?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Rosie's back from honeymoon. Her dad would like to know when the first anniversary party is.",
